 Note: this endpoint was previously named `/v1/saregister`. The old name is still accepted for backwards compatibility.
 
+`/v1/ns/unregister`
+-------------------
+
+This endpoint unregisters an account, with the same semantics as `NS UNREGISTER` (or `NS ERASE`): the account's clients are disconnected and the channels it founded are unregistered. The request is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `accountName`: string, name of the account
+* `erase`: boolean, optional: also delete the record that keeps an unregistered account's name reserved, allowing it to be registered again (like `NS ERASE`)
+
+The response is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `success`: whether the account was unregistered
+* `errorCode`: string, optional, machine-readable description of the error. Possible values include: `ACCOUNT_DOES_NOT_EXIST`, `UNKNOWN_ERROR`.
+
 `/v1/rehash`
 ------------
 
